    "body": "# Bug report\n\n### Bug description:\n\nLeakSanitizer detects memory leaks in the `test__interpchannels` test module. The leaks occur in `_PyXIData_New()` function called from `channel_send()` in `Modules/_interpchannelsmodule.c`.\n\n**Affected versions:**\n- Python 3.13\n- Python 3.14  \n- Python main branch\n\n**Steps to reproduce:**\n\n1. Build Python with address sanitizer:\n```bash\nCC=clang CXX=clang++ ./configure --with-address-sanitizer --with-pydebug --with-undefined-behavior-sanitizer --disable-optimizations && make -j$(nproc)\n```\n\n2. Run the test:\n```bash\n./python -X dev -X showrefcount -m test test__interpchannels -j$(nproc)\n```\n\n**Expected behavior:**\nNo memory leaks detected.\n\n**Actual behavior:**\nLeakSanitizer reports multiple direct memory leaks. The exact number of leaked bytes and allocations varies between Python versions.\n\n**Problematic code locations:**\n\nAll leaks originate from `_PyXIData_New()`:\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/blob/d86ad870cc112d4bd36165398368826746555730/Python/crossinterp.c#L306-L314\n\nCalled through:\n\n1. **`channel_send()`**:\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/blob/d86ad870cc112d4bd36165398368826746555730/Modules/_interpchannelsmodule.c#L1773-L1819\n\n2. **`channel_send_wait()`**:\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/blob/d86ad870cc112d4bd36165398368826746555730/Modules/_interpchannelsmodule.c#L1843-L1894\n\n3. **`_sharednsitem_set_value()`**:\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/blob/d86ad870cc112d4bd36165398368826746555730/Python/crossinterp.c#L2065-L2084\n\n4. **`_copy_string_obj_raw()`** via `_PyXI_InitFailure()`:\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/blob/d86ad870cc112d4bd36165398368826746555730/Python/crossinterp.c#L1041-L1065\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/blob/d86ad870cc112d4bd36165398368826746555730/Python/crossinterp.c#L1805-L1825\n\n**Analysis:**\n\nThe allocated memory in `_PyXIData_New()` is not being properly freed. The function allocates memory using `_PyMem_DebugRawAlloc()` but the corresponding cleanup appears to be missing in error paths or normal execution flow.\n\n**Full leak reports:**\nSee attached log files for detailed stack traces on Python 3.13, 3.14, and main branch.\n\n[313.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22986043/313.log)\n[314.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22986042/314.log)\n[main.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22986044/main.log)\n\n### CPython versions tested on:\n\n3.13, 3.14, CPython main branch\n\n### Operating systems tested on:\n\nLinux\n\n<!-- gh-linked-prs -->\n### Linked PRs\n* gh-140307\n* gh-140338\n* gh-140357\n* gh-140397\n<!-- /gh-linked-prs -->\n",
